'''Gennadiy Vladimirovich Borisov''' ({{langx|ru|Генна́дий Влади́мирович Бори́сов}}; born 1962 in [[Kramatorsk]]){{r|RusskayaPlaneta}} is a Crimean<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/12/07/science/interstellar-comet-2i-borisov.html |title=The Interstellar Comet Has Arrived in Time for the Holidays |last=Overbye |first=Dennis |work=[[The New York Times]] |date=7 December 2019 |access-date=25 March 2020}}</ref> [[amateur telescope making|telescope maker]] and [[amateur astronomy|amateur astronomer]] who discovered the first-known [[interstellar comet]], [[2I/Borisov]], in 2019.

== Work ==
Borisov works as an engineer at the {{ill|Crimean Astronomical Station|ru|Крымская лаборатория ГАИШ МГУ}}<ref group=Note>Not to be confused with the [[Crimean Astrophysical Observatory]], which is located right next to it.</ref> of the [[Sternberg Astronomical Institute]] of [[Moscow State University]].{{r|Sky&Telescope}}{{r|StateAstronomicalInstitute}} There, he maintains the telescopes, but does not make observations himself. He also works with Astronomicheskiy Nauchnyy Tsentr JSC, creating experimental telescopes in collaboration with [[Roscosmos]].{{r|Fontanka.ru}}

